itive crew atmosphere (crew cooperation). Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas (crew cooperation), egocentric (crew cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability). So C seems strong on reliability and decision quality, but weak on communication and adaptability.\n\nD: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience?), concentration, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: arrogant, weak leadership. So D has good responsibility and problem solving, but arrogance may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe can argue that B still seems best overall, but we need to discuss C and D. So we can say: I agree with Agent 3 that B is currently strongest, but we should also evaluate C and D. Provide some facts. Then give provisional vote for B.\n\nThus public message: agree with B, note that C has reliability and decision quality but communication issues, D has responsibility but arrogance, so B remains best. Provide explicit facts.\n\nMetadata JSON: vote B.\n\nProceed."}
